From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: tolerate per-band enrich failure in iface_get_mlsta_info

iface_get_mlsta_info() enriches each link of a multi-link station with
band-specific data from hostapd. When that call fails for one link -- which
happens whenever the client is not currently readable on that link's band --
the WARN_ON(ret) return discarded the entire reply, so a client associated on
a single link was reported as no client at all. The controller sta table then
stayed empty and steering returned Invalid argument.

Keep the nl80211 data already gathered for the link and skip only the failed
enrichment, matching the tolerance the sibling iface_get_mlsta_4addr_info()
already has.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
@@ -1939,8 +1939,15 @@
 				memcpy(sta->bssid, aplinks[j].macaddr, 6);
 
 				ret = iface_get_sta_info_band(ifname, aplinks[j].band, macaddr, sta);
-				if (WARN_ON(ret))
-					return ret;
+				if (ret) {
+					/* Hostapd band enrichment can fail for a link the
+					 * client is not readable on; keep the nl80211 data
+					 * for this link instead of discarding the whole
+					 * multi-link reply. */
+					libwifi_dbg("[%s] %s: band %d enrich failed, keeping nl80211 link data\n",
+						ifname, __func__, aplinks[j].band);
+					break;
+				}
 
 				if (!(sta->caps.valid & WIFI_CAP_EHT_VALID))
 					mlsta->mlo_capable = false;
